  "limitations": [
    "Previously seen fixed PCM; no new held-out quality validation. Original outputs, model locks, scorers, quality thresholds and release gates unchanged.",
    "Only CPU frontend execution and array zero padding are observed. Native chunk scheduling is an explicitly source-derived integer replay; neither native DiarStream nor its neural graph or cache executes.",
    "No learned projection, attention, upsampler, classifier, probability generation, cache compression or model instantiation occurs. No causal claim about probability differences or DER follows.",
    "HF final-call and native final-call global starts can differ for short inputs; common Mel comparisons use explicit global coordinates and every full stack domain is retained separately.",
    "The native256-sample geometric decay is copied from pinned finish source for the FE control; actual output float values are retained, not assumed bitwise-equal to ideal zeros.",
    "Shared native bank is a fixed diagnostic intervention, not a selected release filterbank. Existing own-bank measurements remain unchanged.",
    "Full raw PCM/features/stacks/masks remain outside Git with exact hashes. Metadata, source identities, build record, commands and independently recomputed framing reports are collected separately."
  ],
